  "body": "## What\n\nBrings the docs and screenshots current with the My Claude Code rebrand (v5.0.0) which had left README, docs/USAGE, ARCHITECTURE, the in-dashboard Guide, and all dashboard screenshots showing the old Free Claude Code / `fcc-*` surface.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **README.md, docs/USAGE.md, ARCHITECTURE.md** — `fcc-*` command references → `mcc-*` (legacy aliases noted); version pin `4.16.0` → `5.5.1`; `WEBSEARCH_LOG_CONTENT_MAX_CHARS` `50000` → `2000000`.\n- **In-dashboard Guide** (`admin_static/index.html`, Guide text only) — `mcc-claude`/`mcc-codex`/`mcc-pi`/`mcc-compact-log` with legacy-alias notes.\n- **Screenshots retaken** against the current v5.5.1 UI (Midnight theme, MC mark, readable websearch result cards) on a throwaway server with a fake home. Both `assets/` and `admin_static/img/` copies updated. New `admin-websearch-analytics.png` added.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 112 docs/brand/admin tests pass.\n- Throwaway server stopped (port 8161 free), fake home removed.\n- Built with `/ui-ux-pro-max` (screenshot-consistency reference) + `/chrome-devtools-mcp` (browser driving).\n\n## Not retaken (out of scope)\n\nTerminal/desktop-app captures (`cc-model-picker.png`, `codex*.png`, `claude-desktop-*.png`, `pic.png`) still show v4-era UI — they require capturing the real Claude Code/Codex/Claude Desktop UIs, not the admin browser. Flagged for a future pass.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- Concurrent-agent interference during screenshot capture was mitigated with an isolated browser context; the analytics/websearch shots were re-verified for real data.\n- Binary PNGs are hard to diff; the new sizes (116-215KB at 1600x949) are consistent with real dashboard captures.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
